arbeitnow:senior-software-engineer-permi:
&lt;p&gt;Sony Music’s&lt;strong&gt; Product, Design, Engineering and Global Operations (PDEGO)&lt;/strong&gt; team is&amp;nbsp;looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer to join our Permissions Platform team&lt;/strong&gt; in our&amp;nbsp;King’s Cross London office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Engineer, you’ll collaborate with the team lead to shape the technical direction and delivery of products that empower artists and record labels around the&amp;nbsp;world. You’ll combine hands-on engineering with technical leadership, working closely&amp;nbsp;with Product, Design, and Engineering partners to turn complex needs into reliable,&amp;nbsp;scalable solutions. You’ll build performant scalable solutions, collaborate with other&amp;nbsp;engineers, and help your team deliver meaningful outcomes for our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoMsg_Job"&gt;
&lt;div class="iCIMS_Expandable_Container"&gt;
&lt;div class="iCIMS_Expandable_Text"&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you'll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;● Collaborate on the technical design and delivery of products within a&amp;nbsp;cross-functional team, connecting engineering decisions to user needs and&amp;nbsp;business priorities.&lt;br&gt;● Develop across our technology stack, writing clean, tested, maintainable code&amp;nbsp;and setting a high standard for engineering quality.&lt;br&gt;● Balance scalability, reliability, security, and performance with pragmatic&amp;nbsp;delivery.&lt;br&gt;● Partner closely with Product and Design to understand requirements, assess&amp;nbsp;trade-offs, and break complex initiatives into clear, achievable milestones.&lt;br&gt;● Participate in technical design discussions and code reviews, communicating&amp;nbsp;decisions clearly and building alignment within your team.&lt;br&gt;● Drive improvements to testing, observability, deployment practices, and&amp;nbsp;operational reliability.&lt;br&gt;● Share knowledge and contribute to a collaborative culture of continuous&amp;nbsp;learning and technical ownership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class="iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoField_Job"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;● You bring 8+ years of software engineering experience.&lt;br&gt;● You have a strong track record of building and delivering full-stack web&amp;nbsp;applications; we use TypeScript, React, GraphQL, and Python.&lt;br&gt;● You have experience designing microservices and APIs, with a strong&amp;nbsp;understanding of REST, HTTP, OAuth, and related standards.&lt;br&gt;● You bring strong knowledge of AWS cloud technologies and experience building&amp;nbsp;and operating reliable production services.&lt;br&gt;● You understand how to improve application performance, page load times, and&amp;nbsp;reliability.&lt;br&gt;● You champion automated testing, including unit and integration tests, and&amp;nbsp;practical engineering standards that help teams deliver confidently.&lt;br&gt;● You communicate clearly with technical and non-technical partners, explaining&amp;nbsp;complex ideas and helping teams make informed decisions.&lt;br&gt;● You’re comfortable working in an agile, product-led environment, navigating&amp;nbsp;ambiguity, and balancing longer-term technical goals with immediate priorities.&lt;br&gt;● You enjoy mentoring others and creating an environment where engineers can&amp;nbsp;contribute ideas, take ownership, and grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class="iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoField_Job"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we give you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;● A competitive salary and bonus scheme.&lt;br&gt;● Music perks, including free vinyl, gig tickets, live shows in our office, and&amp;nbsp;opportunities to skip the queue at major UK festivals.&lt;br&gt;● An office environment with breathwork, yoga, and Pilates classes; monthly craft&amp;nbsp;sessions, including perfume making, pottery, and sushi rolling; pub quizzes; and&amp;nbsp;album and single launches.&lt;br&gt;● An on-site restaurant for breakfast and lunch, plus on-site baristas across two&amp;nbsp;floors.&lt;br&gt;● Private healthcare and dental cover, with the option to include your family.&lt;br&gt;● 25 days of annual leave, plus bank holidays and our winter recess.&lt;br&gt;● Regular social activities, including drinks, running clubs, football teams, fantasy&amp;nbsp;football, gigs, and a movie club.&lt;br&gt;● Quarterly PDEGO socials, including bowling, Formula 1, karaoke, and bingo.&lt;br&gt;● Discounts across other Sony brands, including electronics and movies.&lt;br&gt;● Entertainment and dining discounts through Tastecard, NightKey, and Gourmet&amp;nbsp;Society.&lt;br&gt;● Opportunities to contribute to Sony Music’s Social Justice Fund.&lt;br&gt;● An inclusive, collaborative, global community where you can help fuel the&amp;nbsp;creative journey.&lt;br&gt;● A modern office environment designed to support productivity, creativity, and&amp;nbsp;teamwork.&lt;br&gt;● A generous pension scheme, life assurance, and income protection.&lt;br&gt;● Investment in your professional growth and development.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class="iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoField_Job"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Sony Music Entertainment, we fuel the creative journey. We’ve played a pioneering role in music history, from the first-ever music label to the invention of the flat disc record. We’ve nurtured some of music’s most iconic artists and produced some of the most influential recordings of all time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, we work in more than 70 countries, supporting a diverse roster of international superstars, developing and independent artists, and visionary creators. From our position at the intersection of music, entertainment, and technology, we bring imagination and expertise to the newest products and platforms, embrace new business models, employ breakthrough tools, and provide powerful insights that help our artists push creative boundaries and reach new audiences. In everything we do, we’re committed to artistic integrity, transparency, and entrepreneurship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Music Entertainment is a member of the Sony family of global companies.&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class="iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoField_Job"&gt;&lt;strong style="font-size: 14px;"&gt;Equal Opportunities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an active part of a culturally and socially diverse society, Sony Music’s aim is that our workforce is diverse and inclusive. Sony Music is an equal opportunity employer and supports workforce diversity.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We employ, retain, promote and otherwise treat all employees and job applicants according to their merit, qualifications, competence and talent. We apply this policy without regard to any individual’s sex, race, religion, origin, age, sexual orientation, marital status, medical condition or disability.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please click&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="http://tools.sonymusiccreative.com/privacy/PCP_UK.pdf" target="_blank"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to read our privacy policy before beginning the application process as you will need to agree to the terms of the policy before submitting your information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note that applicants must be at least 18 years of age.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</p>

